It's simple, reliable, resource-based.

54
00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.100
But sometimes REST gives you way too much data,

55
00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.420
which creates a problem called overfetching.

56
00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.520
GraphQL solves this beautifully

57
00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.900
by letting the client ask for the exact specific data points it needs

58
00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.600
in one single request. It's like going to a buffet and only getting exactly what you want to eat.

